## Highlights

- **Install a real Mac or Ubuntu application.** The headline change from [PR #289](https://github.com/ThisIs-Developer/Markdown-Viewer/pull/289) adds Finder-ready DMGs for Intel, Apple Silicon, and Universal Macs plus dependency-aware DEB packages and optional portable archives for three Linux architectures.
- **Trust the package you selected.** Release assembly now rejects missing, unexpected, empty, or non-file assets, verifies every checksum before publication, and ships platform identity, installation, signing-status, and SHA-256 guidance beside the downloads.
- **Work more naturally with files and folders.** Import browser folders, rename Explorer items inline, download selected documents or a complete folder as ZIP, and recover linked-file renames without losing newer drafts.
- **Copy Preview content with its real appearance.** Rich clipboard output now retains computed typography, backgrounds, borders, code styling, list numbering, safe links, and precise partial selections while staying compact.
- **Return to the same reading position.** Preview scroll survives skeleton loading, tab changes, hidden panes, image settlement, and Editor/Preview view switches without an obsolete render moving another document.
- **Choose the PDF result you need.** **Standard PDF (Recommended)** preserves selectable, searchable text; **Rendered PDF** produces consistent image-based pages. Long paragraphs, tables, code, lists, images, and repeated headers no longer lose content at page boundaries.

